#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
#, sh-format
msgid "OpenTabletDriver drives most drawing tablets, Wacom, Huion, XP-Pen, Gaomon and many more, the same way on every one: pressure, the pen's buttons, and which part of the screen the tablet covers. This installs it from Flathub, and copies its udev rules from its ${OTD_TAG} release into /etc so that it can reach the tablet. It turns off the kernel's own tablet drivers (wacom, hid_uclogic), which would take the tablet first: if one already has, restart."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
msgid "It moves the pointer through /dev/uinput, which the image keeps from apps: a virtual keyboard can type into any window. This gives it back to whoever sits at the machine (ame security virtual-input), and so to every app that may reach all of /dev, the Chromium browsers among them."
