#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
msgid "This machine is sealed: its kernel arguments are inside the signed kernel image, and firmware kept outside the image would not be covered by its seal. The adapter cannot be set up here; Xbox controllers still work over Bluetooth or a USB cable."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
#, sh-format
msgid "Microsoft's wireless adapter for Xbox controllers, and the one some laptops have built in, needs Microsoft's firmware, which the image may not pass on. This downloads Microsoft's driver packages from its update catalog, checks each against the checksum pinned in the image, and keeps the firmware in ${FIRMWARE}, where the kernel looks first from the next restart. The firmware is subject to Microsoft's Terms of Use: https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/legal/terms-of-use"
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
msgid "The adapter is a MediaTek MT7612U chip, and Linux's Wi-Fi driver for that chip (mt76x2u) would take it first, so this keeps that driver from loading: a USB Wi-Fi stick with the same chip (Netgear A6210 and many AC1200 sticks) stops working until ame apps xbox-adapter off."
msgstr ""

