#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
msgid "The Arch User Repository (AUR) is build scripts, PKGBUILDs, that anyone can upload and nobody reviews, and malware has been found in it more than once. What you build from it runs as you, with your files, your display and your session, as anything in a container does."
msgstr ""

#: usr/share/amethystora/just/apps.just
msgid "Turned on, amethystora-pkg offers the arch-aur template, whose containers keep their settings in a home folder of their own, and the paru manager. Before anything is built it shows what the AUR knows of it: who maintains it, how many vote for it, how old it is, whether it is flagged out of date. paru then shows you the PKGBUILD itself: read it. Packages from the AUR are never upgraded unattended."
msgstr ""

